{"translation": "The matter [347] of rest, then, is clear. For as exercises naturally dry, so rest, which is quiet and absence of exercise, naturally preserves the moistures. Food, however, does not moisten simply by being more abundant; that food moistens which is without a strong quality, that is, neither astringent nor acrid nor salty nor bitter. We have sometimes given radishes in oxymel, having fixed shoots of white hellebore into them for a whole day and night, and such a purging from hellebore would be a weak one. Those who have the thorax narrow and for this reason also compressed are the most unsuitable of all for purgations by means of emetic drugs, both the others and above all those by means of white hellebore. For in them some one of the vessels in the respiratory organs ruptures. One must also evacuate the bitter-bilious humour upwards and the phlegm downwards. There are times, however, when it is the reverse, if a phlegmatic humour has collected in the stomach and a bitter-bilious one in the intestines. The melancholic humour, however, must always be evacuated downwards.", "renderings": [{"target_no": 14, "surface": "ἀνάπαυσις,", "english": "rest", "uncertain": "n"}, {"target_no": 20, "surface": "ἀγυμνασία,", "english": "absence of exercise", "uncertain": "n"}, {"target_no": 35, "surface": "ποιότητος", "english": "quality", "uncertain": "n"}, {"target_no": 44, "surface": "ἁλυκὴ", "english": "salty", "uncertain": "n"}, {"target_no": 60, "surface": "ἑλλεβόρου", "english": "hellebore", "uncertain": "n"}, {"target_no": 110, "surface": "ἀναπνευστικοῖς", "english": "respiratory", "uncertain": "n"}, {"target_no": 116, "surface": "πικρόχολον", "english": "bitter-bilious", "uncertain": "n"}, {"target_no": 133, "surface": "φλεγματικὸς,", "english": "phlegmatic humour", "uncertain": "n"}], "uncertain_greek": ["στέρνον (apparently corrupt; translated as if στενόν, 'narrow')", "ἔχοντε (read as ἔχοντες)", "πήξαντες (taken as 'having fixed/stuck' the hellebore shoots into the radishes)", "δι’ ὀξυμέλιτος (taken as 'in oxymel')"]}
